# Every text file is checked out with LF, whatever the platform or the user's
# core.autocrlf. With autocrlf=true on Windows, git otherwise rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF, which breaks shell scripts ("\r: command not found"),
# bakes \r into Dockerfile RUN lines, and makes gofmt flag every Go file. The
# stored blobs are already LF, so this changes checkouts only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Committed build artifacts embedded with go:embed (pkg/trampoline/trampoline.bin,
# pkg/preload/libepochd_preload.so). Never touch their bytes; do not rely on
# git's content sniffing to leave them alone.
*.so  binary
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
